{
  "q1_accurate": [
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "pebble.Batch (callers)", "note": "composed_by listed all six direct holders (indexedBatch batch.go:488, batchIter batch.go:1761, commitQueue commit.go:25, iteratorBatchState iterator.go:392, metamorphic.Test, replay.workloadStep) with correct line numbers; all cited"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "pebble.Batch", "note": "retained_via_interfaces ring located wal.recordQueueEntry/poppedEntry (failover_writer.go:22,29), ConcurrencyLimitScheduler (compaction_scheduler.go:260), keyspan.InterleavingIterOpts via SpanMask->rangeKeyMasking, internalIterOpts boundLimitedFilter, iterv2.InterleavingIter, invalidating.iter, bench.ycsb — 8 of 14 rows verified real and cited"},
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "RefCount", "note": "found wal.RefCount (wal/wal.go:434) and pebble.Batch.Ref (batch.go:291), pinning Batch as the concrete RefCount carrier"},
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "rangeKeyMasking", "note": "located range_keys.go:227 struct and its init method, leading to the parent *Iterator field at range_keys.go:244"},
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "write batch type callers build up writes before committing", "note": "correctly oriented to batch.go and DB.commitWrite db.go:891 in Step 1"}
  ],
  "q1_wrong": [
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "pebble.rangeKeyMasking.init (callers)", "note": "returned zero callers with verdict 'complete' — actually called at db.go:1248 and external_iterator.go:240 (method-on-field dispatch); the 'complete resolvable edge set — do not re-grep' advice was actively misleading"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "pebble.Batch", "note": "3 of 14 retained_via_interfaces rows were false positives I had to disprove at source: record.Writer via flusher carrier bench.pebbleDB (nonsensical chain), keyspan.SpanIterOptions via BlockPropertyFilter (options.go:325-331 carries only RangeKeyFilters), compact.Iter<-batchIter (no injection site exists)"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "pebble.Batch", "note": "missed the two most critical retainers: mergingIterLevel.iter (db.go:1435, batchIter behind internalIterator) and flushableBatch.data aliasing Batch.data behind the flushable interface (batch.go:1977/2009) — both found only via rg/read"}
  ],
  "q2_fallbacks": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "pebble.Batch", "fallback": "read", "missing": "injection/construction lines — the ring names the holder struct and carrier but not the site where the field gets the batch-derived value (db.go:908/950 WriteRecord, db.go:1312 Mask:, db.go:1377 boundLimitedFilter all required reading source)"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "pebble.Batch", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "[]byte-typed aliasing (flushableBatch.data) and interface-embedded holders (flushableEntry embeds flushable) are invisible to the retention ring"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "pebble.rangeKeyMasking.init", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "callers entirely (empty edge set with 'complete' verdict); rg found db.go:1248 instantly"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "pebble.Batch.Ref", "fallback": "read", "missing": "the call site that passes *Batch as wal.RefCount — graph callers of Ref were noise (Version.Ref, FileCache.Ref); the actual injection at db.go:950 came from reading commitWrite"},
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "InterleavingIterOpts", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "goroutine-crossing evidence (go statements: log_writer.go:595, failover_manager.go:336, compaction.go:1389) — Sense has no concept of go-statement edges, all required rg"}
  ],
  "q3_hints": [
    {"tool": "read", "query_before": "reading db.go/scan_internal.go file-by-file", "query_after": "sense_search keyword 'rangeKeyMasking' then rg for literal sites", "hint": "'You have read 6 files. Stop reading file by file and navigate structurally with Sense' — pushed me to structural search, though I ultimately needed rg for injection sites Sense couldn't express"},
    {"tool": "grep", "query_before": "grep 'RefCount'", "query_after": "sense_search keyword 'RefCount'", "hint": "grep tool refusal: 'Use the Sense MCP tools for symbol or structural lookups instead of grep/glob' — the redirected sense_search worked well here"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query_before": "sense_graph pebble.Batch", "query_after": "sense_blast pebble.Batch", "hint": "next_steps: 'run sense_blast for full change impact and what holds it (retained_via_interfaces, holders that keep it behind an interface and never name it)' — this was exactly the audit's core need"}
  ],
  "q4_value": "sense_blast's retained_via_interfaces ring: 14 candidate interface-laundered holders with carrier chains (e.g. rangeKeyMasking > Iterator > iteratorBatchState > Batch) in one call — enumerating that ring manually would have taken dozens of greps, and rows like the WAL failover RefCount carrier and the compaction scheduler's DBForCompaction were genuine 'cannot see via field-type sweep' finds.",
  "q5_improve": "Attach the injection site to each retained_via_interfaces row — the file:line where the carrier is actually assigned into the interface-typed field (or flag it as 'satisfier-match only, no assignment site found'). That one addition would have separated the 8 real rows from the 3 false positives automatically and eliminated most of my rg/read verification passes; also, don't claim 'complete' on caller graphs that miss method-on-field dispatch (rangeKeyMasking.init).",
  "score": 7,
  "score_rationale": "Band 7-8: the retained_via_interfaces ring and composed_by genuinely accelerated the audit and surfaced non-greppable carrier chains, but per Q1-Q2 the two highest-risk retainers (flushableBatch.data alias, mergingIterLevel) were missed entirely, 3 ring rows were false positives, and a 'complete'-verdict graph returned zero callers for a called method — so every Sense claim still required a grep/read fallback to confirm."
}
